  "text": "The discussion about how things relate to each other is a major focus today, and the ways people think about it can be grouped into three broad categories. The first viewpoint holds that nothing has an inherent, fixed character; all positions, durations, and movements are defined only in relation to other things. This idea is very old, tracing back to early philosophical thought, and most people accept it, although a small minority still hope for the existence of an absolute frame of reference, a fixed backdrop, or a true state of stillness. Even the notion of truth is seen as dependent on perspective, echoing the skeptical question about the nature of truth itself."
